# Slot-value exclusion for the {word} slot of Spell.intent (OVOS-INTENT-2 §4.3:
# a .blacklist paired by base name with a slot lists values that MUST NOT fill
# it, leaving the slot unresolved rather than binding them).
#
# Concrete conflict: utterances like "how do you spell it", "spell them" or
# "can you spell this" would otherwise bind the anaphoric pronoun as {word} and
# the skill would dutifully spell out "I-T" / "T-H-E-M". Excluding the pronouns
# leaves {word} unresolved so a later stage resolves the referent
# (OVOS-CONTEXT-1 §7 context fill) or the skill re-prompts for the actual word.
#
# One phrase per line (BlacklistFile.load() only expands a line that contains
# an inline "<vocab>" reference; parenthesised alternations like "(a|b)" are
# NOT expanded here and would otherwise be stored and matched as a single
# literal string, silently disabling the exclusion).
#
# Pronoun sets are language-specific, hence kept here in locale/en-US/ rather
# than in engine code (OVOS-INTENT-2 §4.3).
it
this
that
these
those
he
she
they
him
her
them
his
hers
their
theirs
i
me
my
mine
you
your
yours
we
us
our
ours
